    "response": "**Most Diverse Colleges in Arizona:**\n\n* **Arizona State University (ASU)**:\n    * Overall: 7th most diverse in the U.S.\n    * Black or African American: 13.3%\n    * Hispanic or Latino: 29.6%\n    * Asian American: 17.1%\n    * Native American: 2.8%\n    * International: 13.6%\n* **University of Arizona (UArizona)**:\n    * Overall: 150th most diverse in the U.S.\n    * Black or African American: 6.2%\n    * Hispanic or Latino: 28.1%\n    * Asian American: 12.2%\n    * Native American: 2.4%\n    * International: 11.5%\n* **Northern Arizona University (NAU)**:\n    * Overall: 172nd most diverse in the U.S.\n    * Black or African American: 3.2%\n    * Hispanic or Latino: 22.8%\n    * Asian American: 10.9%\n    * Native American: 11.7%\n    * International: 2.4%\n* **Grand Canyon University (GCU)**:\n    * Overall: 239th most diverse in the U.S.\n    * Black or African American: 13.1%\n    * Hispanic or Latino: 19.6%\n    * Asian American: 6.7%\n    * Native American: 2.6%\n    * International: 3.4%\n* **University of Phoenix** (Main Campus):\n    * Overall: 343rd most diverse in the U.S.\n    * Black or African American: 32.5%\n    * Hispanic or Latino: 33.1%\n    * Asian American: 10.2%\n    * Native American: 2.1%\n    * International: 4.8%\n\n**Notes:**\n\n* Diversity rankings are based on the 2022-2023 College Factual rankings.\n* Overall diversity includes the percentage of students who identify as Black or African American, Hispanic or Latino, Asian American, Native American, and international.\n* The University of Phoenix also has additional campuses with varying diversity profiles.",
